-- title:
--   Smooth proper ℤ_{(ℓ)}-model of X₀(p) with finite-map data
-- statement:
--   Let $p \ge 1$ be an integer, let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid p$, and write $R = \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. The assertion is the existence of the following package. A scheme $X$ with a morphism $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ that is proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; a section $\varepsilon$ of $c$; for every $m_0$ a datum $\mathfrak{F}$ of type `SmoothProperCurve.FiniteMapData c ε` with $m_0 \le \mathfrak{F}.m$ and satisfying `LevelSetsGenericallyEtale`, that is, two affine opens $U, V$ covering $X$ with $U$ the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, sections $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$, $g \in \Gamma(X,V)$ with $U \cap V$ the basic open of each and $fg = 1$ there, both $R[T] \to \Gamma(X,U)$, $T \mapsto f$ and $R[T] \to \Gamma(X,V)$, $T \mapsto g$ finite, all level algebras $S \otimes_R \Gamma(X,U)/(1\otimes f - s\otimes 1)$ free of rank $\mathfrak{F}.m$ over a local $R$-algebra $S$, and étale over $S$ whenever $D(s)$ is a unit for a fixed polynomial $D \in R[T]$ having a unit coefficient. Next, a curve model $M_\eta$ (an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over the base field, with function field identified with the given field and closed points in bijection with places, the stalks matching the valuation rings) of $\bar F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, the compositum of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with the field $F_0 =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` generated by the $q$-expansions of $j(q^d)$, $d \mid p$, inside Laurent series; an isomorphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ onto $X \times_{R} \operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with the structure maps; Galois equivariance, namely that if the $X$-components of two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x', x$ of $M_\eta$ differ by $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ for $g \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, then the place of $x'$ is the translate of the place of $x$ by the semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois` of $\bar F$ attached to $g$. Further, a curve model $M_0$ of $F_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with an isomorphism $e_0$ onto $X \times_R \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$ over the structure maps, compatible with $e_\eta$ in the sense that if a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $y$ of $X_{\mathbb{Q}}$ has the same $X$-component as a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $x$ of $M_\eta$ and specialises under $e_0^{-1}$ to a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$, then the valuation subring of the place of $x$, restricted along $F_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} F_0 \cong \bar F$, is the valuation subring of $M_0$'s place at $x_0$. Finally, for each valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, a ring homomorphism $\rho_A : R \to A$ lifting $R \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a curve model $M_A$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField A) p` over the residue field of $A$, and an isomorphism of $M_A.C$ with $X \times_R \operatorname{Spec}(\operatorname{ResidueField} A)$ over the structure maps. For every such $A$ whose residue field is algebraically closed, the conclusion provides a map $r$ from places of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of the modular function field over the residue field which satisfies `IsPlaceReductionModL` (it preserves degrees, and for a Laurent series over $A$ lying in $\bar F$ whose reduction lies in the residual modular function field and is nonzero, $r$ pushes the divisor forward to the divisor of the reduction), and which computes specialisation geometrically: for every $A$-point $x_A$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_A)$, every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $x$ of $M_\eta$ with $X$-component the generic point of $x_A$, and every residue-field point $y$ of $M_A$ with $X$-component the special point of $x_A$, the place of $y$ is $r$ applied to the place of $x$.
--
--   This is the arithmetic model statement for the modular curve $X_0(p)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for $\ell \nmid p$, in the form used later in the construction of the Jacobian $J_0(p)$: a smooth proper relative curve with a section, equipped with chart-wise finite maps to the affine line of arbitrarily large degree and generically étale level sets, together with identifications of its geometric generic fibre, its rational generic fibre and its fibres modulo places above $\ell$ with models of the corresponding modular function fields, the last identification realising reduction of points as Deuring's reduction of places. It is cited by the constructions of the abelian-scheme model of $J_0(p)$, of the cotangent comparison for its torsion, and of the point dictionaries for the rational fibre.
